Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "UrbanDrivingWithFogAndVehicleAnomaly" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :vehicle1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :foggyCondition1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:vehicle1 a :Vehicle ;
    :description "Black sedan driving in foggy conditions" .

:foggyCondition1 a :FoggyCondition .

:risk1 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to fog, increasing risk of collision with unseen obstacles" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision risk due to limited visibility of surrounding vehicles and pedestrians" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Wet road conditions due to fog, increasing risk of skidding or loss of vehicle control" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.9"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Reduced visibility due to fog, increasing risk of collision with unseen obstacles
Severity Score: 0.9

**Risk 2:**
Description: Potential collision risk due to limited visibility of surrounding vehicles and pedestrians
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 3:**
Description: Wet road conditions due to fog, increasing risk of skidding or loss of vehicle control
Severity Score: 0.75

---
The scene is classified as a **StateAnomaly** due to the foggy conditions causing reduced visibility and potential hazardous driving conditions. The primary risks identified are **OcclusionRisk**, **CollisionRisk**, and **RoadConditionRisk**. The severity scores reflect the high risk associated with foggy conditions, particularly in urban driving scenarios.